WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.787
Unit 1 is the government-cloud
fact that shapes this gate.

2
00:00:03.787 --> 00:00:07.988
Microsoft Learn's page on Security
Exposure Management says it's

3
00:00:07.988 --> 00:00:11.800
available in Public Cloud only,
not in U S Government clouds.

4
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.363
That's the product that
holds attack paths,

5
00:00:14.363 --> 00:00:17.438
the exposure graph and
critical asset management.

6
00:00:17.438 --> 00:00:22.837
Learn doesn't name G C C explicitly, but
Defender for U S Government customers,

7
00:00:22.837 --> 00:00:27.465
G C C included, is built in Azure U
S Government, so the guide treats G

8
00:00:27.465 --> 00:00:32.350
C C as not available too, and lists
that as something it couldn't verify.

9
00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:34.503
What the government clouds do have,

10
00:00:34.503 --> 00:00:37.696
from Learn's Defender for
Endpoint government page:

11
00:00:37.696 --> 00:00:42.373
Defender Vulnerability Management, core
and premium, without two features,

12
00:00:42.373 --> 00:00:45.046
report inaccuracy and
request C V E support;

13
00:00:45.046 --> 00:00:48.313
and Secure Score, with some
recommendations missing.

14
00:00:48.313 --> 00:00:51.622
So a Zero Trust Assessment
test that needs Exposure

15
00:00:51.622 --> 00:00:55.624
Management is recorded as not
applicable in the tenant's cloud.

16
00:00:55.624 --> 00:01:00.050
It goes in the closure register as
a disposition, not a failed control.
